# packages/mcp/contracts/*.json are generated artifacts (scripts/generate-contracts.ts)
# byte-compared in schema-contracts.test.ts against plain Node
# JSON.stringify(x, null, 2) output. Prettier's JSON printer collapses
# short arrays onto one line (JSON.stringify never does), so letting
# the pre-commit hook run prettier on these breaks that exact-match test the
# next time any of them gets staged in a commit.
packages/mcp/contracts/*.json

# Same collapse hazard as above, hit for real by coverage-guard.test.ts
# (B3.2, Req 13): coverage-pending.snapshot.json is regenerated via
# `JSON.stringify(pending, null, 2) + "\n"` (always multi-line), but
# prettier's JSON printer collapses a short flat array of strings onto one
# line — which happened the first time this file held more than one key.
packages/mcp/src/__tests__/coverage-guard/coverage-pending.snapshot.json

# Frozen Tier 3 historical-record docs (flatten-version-docs, Req 9): each
# gets exactly one added clarifying banner line and MUST otherwise stay
# byte-identical. None of these were prettier-formatted before, so letting
# the pre-commit hook run prettier on them on next touch would reformat the whole
# file and violate that "exactly one line" contract.
CHANGELOG.md
packages/server/CHANGELOG.md
docs/archive/audits/AUDIT_SPEC_COVERAGE_2026-06.md

# Same collapse hazard again, this time as pure churn: qualification records are
# written by scripts/qualify-harness-host.mjs with JSON.stringify(r, null, 2),
# and prettier collapses their short `observedEvents` array onto one line. Every
# re-qualification then rewrites what the last commit's prettier run flattened,
# so the diff never settles. These files are recorded evidence, not source.
packages/harness/qualifications/*.json

# Archived process docs (plans, specs, audits, finished openspec changes): kept
# as written, so a rename never turns into a reformatting diff.
docs/archive/
